blocks.en:
Our contributions are as follows:
(a) we formulate BPE merge selection as a model selection problem rather than relying on predefined values;
(b) we evaluate several statistical and information-theoretic model selection criteria;
(c) we propose synthetic text augmentation to improve the estimation of token distributions, particularly in low-resource settings;
(d) we provide empirical analyses showing how different selection criteria affect merge inventories, compression efficiency and downstream performance.

blocks.zh:
我们的捐款如下:
(a) 我们把BPE合并选择作为一个模型选择问题,而不是依赖预先定义的数值;
(b) 我们评价若干统计和信息理论模型选择标准;
(c) 我们建议对文字进行综合扩充,以改进对象征性分配的估计,特别是在资源匮乏的情况下;
(d) 我们提供经验分析,说明不同的选择标准如何影响合并清单、压缩效率和下游业绩。

blocks.en:
For each corpus, dataset size, and data condition ( orig , gen , orig+gen ), our experiments rely on the following steps:
(a) construct tokenizers using various selection strategies;
(b) apply the resulting tokenizers to downstream tasks;
(c) evaluate compression and task performance.
All experiments use the same underlying model and inference settings, ensuring that differences in performance arise solely from the choice of tokenizer.

blocks.zh:
对于每个元件,数据集大小,以及数据条件(orig, gen, orig+gen),我们的实验依赖于以下步骤:
(a) 利用各种选择战略建造标定器;
(b) 对下游任务使用由此产生的标定剂;
(c) 评价压缩和任务业绩。
所有实验都使用相同的基础模型和推论设置,确保性能的差异完全源于选择标致剂.
